# Phase 18 live callback executor setting parity — 2026-10-15T13:21:43Z

- Read-only source review against RocketMQ Java 5.5.1 confirmed that
  `NettyRemotingClient.getCallbackExecutor()` checks the retained mutable
  `NettyClientConfig.disableCallbackExecutor` value on each call, and
  `setCallbackExecutor()` stores the supplied executor even while the setting
  is disabled. `NettyRemotingAbstract` obtains the executor at callback
  completion time.
- Rust now stores the disable setting in an atomic live adapter, reads it at
  callback-executor getter/dispatch time, and always retains a supplied
  executor while disabled. Added getter/setter methods and regressions for
  live toggling, inline dispatch while disabled, and executor identity after
  re-enabling. The Java live-config probe covers post-start config mutation
  and executor retention.
- Code commit: `9881c230 fix(remoting): read callback executor disable setting live`.
